WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.992
In the year 618, Emperor Yang of Sui was living in the palace at Jiangdu.

00:00:05.342 --> 00:00:11.126
The palace stood by the river — beautiful, yet very quiet and deserted.

00:00:11.476 --> 00:00:18.076
Emperor Yang was exhausted in body and mind; he drank all day to drown his sorrows, and court affairs fell into neglect.

00:00:18.426 --> 00:00:23.298
The officials dared not say much, and the palace grew quieter and quieter.

00:00:23.648 --> 00:00:28.640
Late one night, the generals of the imperial guard secretly plotted to launch a mutiny.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:32.758
They lowered their voices as they discussed their next move.

00:00:33.108 --> 00:00:39.372
Fires flared up all over the palace, and the guards ran about in panic.

00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:43.922
Shouts and running footsteps shattered the stillness of the deep night.

00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:48.088
The rebels stormed through the palace gate, and Emperor Yang was killed.

00:00:48.438 --> 00:00:54.438
The death of Emperor Yang symbolized that the rule of the Sui dynasty had reached its end.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:01:03.620
Beneath the sunset, the fallen dragon banner and the empty throne told of the end of a dynasty.

